Source provenance

This project's extraction, host controller, packet generator and integration were
prepared for Junyi in October 2026.

ESPARGOS/esp-sdr
https://github.com/ESPARGOS/esp-sdr
Base commit: f86da81807b7f6e850742f6b789d9468c190ad41
Source of ESP32-S3 radio initialization/tuning, DC calibration tracking,
reserved RF SRAM layout and linker guards. The S3-only calibration logic in
main/radio.c is an extraction/adaptation of main/targets/esp32s3/receiver.c,
main/common/rx_recalibration.c, rx_calibration_state.c and rx_lo.h.
GPL-3.0; original license text retained in LICENSE.

cyber-murmel/esp-sdr-zephyr
https://github.com/cyber-murmel/esp-sdr-zephyr
Version v0.1.3, commit prefix 8463f88.
Source of DAC register sequencing, power-ladder entries, and overlapping SRAM
bank playback: lib/esp_sdr/src/esp_sdr_tx.c and esp_sdr_tx_dac.c.
Those sources declare GPL-3.0-or-later.

Both esp-sdr and esp-sdr-zephyr warn that driving the radio through these
private PHY paths is not intended or qualified for productive use and may
permanently alter the radio's analog characteristics. The same warning
applies to this firmware.

Djoko-cli/benq-screenbar-halo-matter
https://github.com/Djoko-cli/benq-screenbar-halo-matter/blob/main/docs/PROTOCOL.md
Reference for Halo 1 frame structure, field interpretation and brightness range.
Protocol observations were compared with locally captured CRC-valid packets.
No controller source code from that project is included.

ESP-IDF
https://github.com/espressif/esp-idf
Pinned commit: 25fe69f946311abdaf9ad56591f25fedbc20ac98
External build dependency. Private PHY ABI and SRAM registers are version-specific.
RMT LED timing follows its documented WS2812 example (0.3/0.9 us).
